Here is the root cause:
The original `ovpn_tcp_rcv` function used `pskb_pull` with large offsets on coalesced skbs from `__strp_rcv`, causing `skb->data - skb->head` to exceed the u16 storage of `skb->network_header`, leading to failure of `skb_reset_network_header` on inner decapsulated packets. Additionally, extracting packets from arbitrary positions within coalesced TCP stream provided no alignment guarantees, causing performance penalties and inherent misalignment of the 4-byte opcode and packet ID fields due to the 2-byte length prefix.

